  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Australia politics live: Telstra pays CEO $6.8m for year despite nationwide outage; Victorian premier tells student protesters against Pauline Hanson to ‘stay in school’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/13/australia-politics-live-news-bargaining-meta-tiktok-housing-migration-question-time-anthony-albanese-angus-taylor-pauline-hanson-labor-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Vicki Brady still paid close to $7m despite 20% of her bonus being docked by the company. Follow today’s news live</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Legislation forcing tech companies to pay for Australian journalism to be introduced</strong></p><p>The government will today introduce its legislation forcing tech companies to pay for journalism in Australia after making a series of 11th-hour changes and reaching an agreement with the Coalition.</p><p>That obligation to enter into at least eight deals is if they want to fully acquit. So it still will be open to tech companies to only partially offset their obligation. But if they want to fully offset their obligation, there have to be at least eight deals. In addition to that obligation, there’s a 200% offset for small and medium players. So that’s also a very strong incentive for them to enter into agreements with regional media, with CALD media and LGBTQI and other smaller players.</p><p>Andrew was sharing his personal views in his speech, the National Press Club. We are going through our policy development process. We’re doing it carefully. We’re doing it deliberately.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/13/australia-politics-live-news-bargaining-meta-tiktok-housing-migration-question-time-anthony-albanese-angus-taylor-pauline-hanson-labor-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-13T00:44:46"
    },
    {
      "title": "Pay with a glance at a screen as biometric technology company begins push into Australian retail",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/13/pay-with-a-glance-at-a-screen-as-biometric-technology-company-begins-push-into-australian-retail",
      "description": "<p>Customers will be able to pay using face and palm scans, potentially speeding up transactions – but rollout of the technology is likely to be slow</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/13/australia-politics-live-news-bargaining-meta-tiktok-housing-migration-question-time-anthony-albanese-angus-taylor-pauline-hanson-labor-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The company behind 300,000 Eftpos terminals across Australia is hoping shoppers will want to make payments by simply glancing at a screen, as biometric technology pushes further into retailing.</p><p>Verifone is selling the innovation as “pay for your coffee with a smile”, promising faster checkouts for people who opt in to having their face or palm-vein – the veins in people’s hands – biometrics used for Eftpos transactions in Australia.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/13/pay-with-a-glance-at-a-screen-as-biometric-technology-company-begins-push-into-australian-retail\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-12T22:30:41"
    },
    {
      "title": "Ignore the doomsdayers – property investing in Australia is far from broken",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/13/property-investors-australia-tax-negative-gearing-rba-interest-rates",
      "description": "<p>Investor loan applications may have fallen since the start of the year, but the slump already appears to be turning around</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Ignore the doomsday warnings about the government’s tax changes – property investing in Australia is a little bruised, but it’s far from broken.</p><p>The country’s biggest mortgage lender, Commonwealth Bank, reported a bumper $11bn full-year cash profit on Wednesday, backed by robust demand for its lending products, especially mortgages.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/13/property-investors-australia-tax-negative-gearing-rba-interest-rates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-12T22:24:28"
    },
    {
      "title": "What’s behind Sydney airport’s heavy delays and near-miss incident?",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/13/whats-behind-sydney-airports-heavy-delays-and-near-miss-incident",
      "description": "<p>Air traffic controllers are short-staffed and exhausted – and new recruits face a difficult aptitude test and must train in Melbourne</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/13/australia-politics-live-news-bargaining-meta-tiktok-housing-migration-question-time-anthony-albanese-angus-taylor-pauline-hanson-labor-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Travellers flying in and out of Sydney airport had already been dealing with heavy delays even before a Jetstar plane <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/10/jetstar-plane-qatar-near-miss-aircraft-proximity-event-sydney-airport\">narrowly avoided colliding with a Qatar Airways plane</a> on the tarmac early on Sunday.</p><p>The day before, more than 150 flights passing through <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/sydney\">Sydney</a> were delayed as the airport grappled with a lack of air traffic controllers, highlighting how just how delicate the rostering situation is.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/13/whats-behind-sydney-airports-heavy-delays-and-near-miss-incident\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-12T15:00:33"
    }
  ]
